# Local-against-cluster dev profile.
#
# Full walkthrough: docs/dev-env.md
# Auth strategy:    docs/authentication.md
#
# Usage:
#   1. Copy:   cp .env.dev.example .env.dev.local
#   2. Fill in the values below (most come from Azure Key Vault — see comments).
#      Or:     scripts/refresh-env.sh dev
#   3. Run:    npm run test:dev           (UI)
#              npm run test:dev:api       (API)
#              APP_ENV=dev npm run test:smoke
#
# ⚠ Never put real secrets in this file. It IS git-trackable (allowed by the
# !.env.*.example rule in .gitignore). Real values go in .env.dev.local.
#
# Profile resolution order (first hit wins):
#   .env.dev.local  ← put your real values here, gitignored
#   .env.dev        ← committed shared defaults (none today)
#   .env.local
#   .env
#
# Pull secrets in one go (after `terraform apply` in bjjeire-terraform-azurerm-aks):
#   TF=/path/to/bjjeire-terraform-azurerm-aks
#   KV=kv-bjjeire-dev-sdc-01
#   cd "$TF"
#   echo "AZURE_TENANT_ID=$(terraform output -raw bjjeire_spa_msal_tenant_id)"
#   echo "AZURE_TESTS_CLIENT_ID=$(terraform output -raw bjjeire_tests_client_id)"
#   echo "AZURE_TESTS_CLIENT_SECRET=$(terraform output -raw bjjeire_tests_client_secret)"
#   echo "AZURE_API_SCOPE=$(terraform output -raw bjjeire_api_audience)/.default"
#   az keyvault secret show --vault-name "$KV" --name bjj-tests-cf-access-client-id     --query value -o tsv
#   az keyvault secret show --vault-name "$KV" --name bjj-tests-cf-access-client-secret --query value -o tsv

# --- Target environment --------------------------------------------------
# npm run test:dev exports APP_ENV=dev before Playwright starts. The copy in
# this file matches what scripts/refresh-env.sh writes.
# Public hostnames exposed via Cloudflare Tunnel + Istio.
APP_ENV=dev
BASE_URL=https://dev.bjjeire.com
API_URL=https://api-dev.bjjeire.com

# --- Entra (tests app registration, client-credentials) ------------------
AZURE_TENANT_ID=
AZURE_TESTS_CLIENT_ID=
AZURE_TESTS_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Application ID URI of the bjjeire-api app registration. The /.default suffix
# is added automatically by the MSAL client if you omit it.
AZURE_API_SCOPE=api://bjjeire-api-dev/.default
# Optional override — defaults to https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant>.
AZURE_AUTHORITY=

# --- Cloudflare Access (service token for non-interactive edge bypass) ---
CF_ACCESS_CLIENT_ID=
CF_ACCESS_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Laptop default is off (headers are still sent when both values above are set).
# CI and in-cluster remote runs default CF_ACCESS_REQUIRED and API_AUTH_REQUIRED to true.
# API_AUTH_REQUIRED=false
# CF_ACCESS_REQUIRED=false

# --- UI test user (browser MSAL flow) ------------------------------------
# Dedicated Entra user from bjjeire-terraform-azurerm-aks
# main.entra-test-user.tf (playwright_test_user_enabled = true on dev,
# forbidden in prod). UPN is playwright-test-<env>@<tenant default domain>.
# Password is random_password.playwright_test_user (force_password_change
# = false) and Key Vault secret bjj-tests-pw-password.
# Terraform does not exclude MFA: add the user to the CA exclusion group
# (recommended name: test-users-no-mfa) by hand.
#
# Today these are populated but UNUSED — listing pages have no in-app MSAL
# redirect. Cloudflare Access is the edge, and tests bypass it with the
# service token above. The auth.setup project that drives the Entra sign-in
# form is gated OFF by PW_UI_ENTRA_AUTH below. See docs/authentication.md.
PW_TEST_USER=
PW_TEST_PASSWORD=

# Set to `true` to enable the Playwright `setup` project that drives the
# browser MSAL sign-in flow. Default false. Flip to true only when the page
# under test actually redirects to Entra. Requires PW_TEST_USER and
# PW_TEST_PASSWORD. Listing pages on dev do not.
PW_UI_ENTRA_AUTH=false

# Pre-built Playwright storageState skips the Entra UI setup project on shards.
# PW_UI_STORAGE_STATE=playwright/.auth/ui-user.json

# --- Misc ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Origin uses a valid public cert (Cloudflare), so leave this false unless
# you're pointing at a host with a self-signed cert.
ACCEPT_INVALID_CERTS=false

# --- Squash TM (docs/squash-tm.md) ---------------------------------------
# Precedence: squash-config.json < these env vars < --squash-* flags.
# A blank value stays unset. Commented lines are valid examples of the other
# forms. Do not uncomment a second publish target: campaign and campaignId
# conflict, and iterationId or testSuiteId stands alone.
#
# Leave MODE blank in this file. Any value loads the Squash reporter for every
# dev run. Pass it per run: SQUASH_TM_MODE=publish npm run squash:sync
# Examples: dry-run (no writes) | publish | auto (publish when CI is detected).
# SQUASH_TM_MODE=dry-run

# Squash root, including the context path. Local stack: squash-tm/docker compose.
SQUASH_TM_URL=http://localhost:8080/squash
# Personal API token: Squash › My account › Personal API tokens (read-write).
# Never commit a real token. Username/password is rejected.
SQUASH_TM_TOKEN=
# Squash project id. 1 is the usual first project.
SQUASH_TM_PROJECT_ID=1

# Only tests carrying this tag are synced. Default @squash.
SQUASH_TM_TAG=@squash
# false: a Squash outage is logged and the suite stays green. CI sets true.
SQUASH_TM_FAIL_ON_ERROR=false
# debug | info | warn | error. debug also prints which source set each key.
SQUASH_TM_LOG_LEVEL=info
# HTTP timeout per Squash call, in milliseconds.
SQUASH_TM_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# Attempts for a retryable Squash call (429, 503, connection refused).
SQUASH_TM_MAX_ATTEMPTS=5

# Folder for new cases no rule matches. Blank: squash-config.json (BjjEire).
SQUASH_TM_TEST_CASE_FOLDER=BjjEire
# Which .env.<profile>.local is read first. Blank: APP_ENV, then local.
# Read from the shell (or dotenv already loaded). A value only inside the
# file it would select cannot change the order.
SQUASH_TM_PROFILE=dev
# Name in "Playwright <environment> <run id>". Blank: APP_ENV, then local.
SQUASH_TM_ENVIRONMENT=dev

# Publish target. This pair finds or creates the campaign and reuses the iteration.
SQUASH_TM_CAMPAIGN=Releases/2.4
SQUASH_TM_ITERATION=Nightly
# An existing campaign id, instead of SQUASH_TM_CAMPAIGN. Do not set both.
# SQUASH_TM_CAMPAIGN_ID=7
# Exactly this iteration. Do not set it together with a campaign or iteration name.
# SQUASH_TM_ITERATION_ID=15
# A test suite picks the tests and receives the results. No campaign or iteration with it.
# SQUASH_TM_TEST_SUITE_ID=3

# true also creates a release execution. false (or blank) updates the test case
# execution only. true/false/1/0/yes/no. A value here applies to every publish;
# --squash-release overrides it for one run.
SQUASH_TM_RELEASE=false
# Run only tests whose Squash case is in this folder or below. Not with a test suite.
# SQUASH_TM_FILTER_FOLDER=BjjEire/Features/Gyms

# Config file. Default squash-config.json. folderRules and projects are file-only;
# SQUASH_TM_FOLDER_RULES and SQUASH_TM_PROJECTS are errors.
SQUASH_TM_CONFIG=squash-config.json

# Set by npm run squash:run / squash:select. Do not set them here.
# SQUASH_TM_CLI={"campaign":"Releases/2.4","iteration":"Nightly"}
# SQUASH_TM_RUNNER=1
# SQUASH_TM_TEST_LIST=playwright/.cache/squash-test-list.txt
